# Assemble v2 (Agile WOW redesign)

Read `docs/redesign/README.md` first, then SPEC.md, COMPONENTS.md, SCREENS.md and WIRING.md.

## Scope

These rules apply to v2 files only. Where they differ from `00-assemble-core.mdc` and
`10-ui-and-a11y.mdc` (radius, product name, navigation, brand colour, RAID log, some vocabulary), v2
wins inside v2 paths until Shane decides each item listed in README "Decisions for Shane". Never
change the existing Datum screens as part of v2 work.

## Must

- Use components from `@/components/assemble-v2`. Add a new one only if no existing component fits;
  then add it to `index.ts`, COMPONENTS.md and `/v2/components`.
- Tokens only: `asm-*` Tailwind utilities from `styles/assemble-v2.css`. No hex in components, no raw
  Tailwind palette classes.
- Status is On track / At risk / Off track, rendered with `StatusPill` (glyph + label + wash). Never
  write "RAG" in the UI.
- Next actions only come from `lib/assemble-v2/next-action.ts`. Change the rule table in SCREENS.md,
  then the code, then the tests.
- Screens render types from `lib/assemble-v2/types.ts`. When wiring, map Prisma to these types in
  `lib/assemble-v2/adapters/`, do not reshape components around database models.
- Server components by default. `'use client'` only for state, browser APIs or navigation hooks.
- Next.js 16: `params` and `searchParams` are Promises; `await` them.
- WCAG 2.2 AA: visible labels, real buttons and links, `aria-labelledby` on cards, focus visible,
  text 4.5:1, charts have a text alternative.
- Copy: UK spelling, sentence case, no em dashes, say what happens. Banned words from
  `30-content-and-copy.mdc` still apply.
- Demo data is fictional. Never add real client names to `demo-data.ts`.

## Must not

- Compute scores or fit in components (use `lib/scoring`).
- Let AI write decisions, statuses or judgements. Co-pilot outputs are drafts until a person saves.
- Build a backlog or sprint board. Read sprint data from Jira or Azure DevOps.
